**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests`

**How to implement.** The preset store and the live Library over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`: … the `LibraryProxy` live view, and the preset … stores'; the S2.3 brief: the preset store holds detectors, polarizers and built-in sources; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row, §4). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs`, `module PresetDatabaseStore`, compiled directly after `SourceDatabaseStore.fs` (step 76): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (a) `type LibraryEntryStore with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : LibraryEntryStore` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, "the SQLite preset store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows")>]`. As in step 69, every field is one `run` over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `LibraryUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. A preset is an entry whose latest row's kind is `DetectorEntryKind` or `PolarizerEntryKind`, or `SourceEntryKind` with a provenance whose `protection` is `ProtectedBuiltIn` (step 24); a user source belongs to the user-sources store (step 76) and a sample to the samples store (step 74). `proxy.entriesForKind kind` decodes (`toSourcePreset`, `toDetectorPreset`, `toPolarizerPreset`, wrapped as `SourceItem`, `DetectorItem`, `PolarizerItem`) the latest version of every preset whose state is `ActiveEntry`, keeps those whose `forKinds` holds the kind, and orders them by name and then by id; `proxy.libraryTrees ()` answers `[ LibraryTree.byKind offered ]` (step 47) over the active presets of every kind in that order; `proxy.tryGetEntry id` answers `None` for an id that is no GUID or names no preset, else the decoded latest version whatever its lifecycle, so a retired preset a table element binds still resolves (001 §B 'Mark `InactiveEntry` (still resolvable)'); `addEntry entry` answers `PresetRefusedErr` naming the entry for a `SampleItem` (the samples store keeps it) and for a `UserManaged` `SourceItem` (the user-sources store keeps it), then `LibraryError.entryAlreadyHeld` (step 77) when any entry holds the id, and otherwise stages `stageNewEntry` of `ofSourcePreset`, `ofDetectorPreset` or `ofPolarizerPreset` at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (step 32, the one built-in catalogue) for a `ProtectedBuiltIn` preset and `UserProvenance` for a `UserManaged` one, because the protection derives from the provenance (step 24); a builder refusal is `PresetRefusedErr` carrying its `describe`. (b) `type LibraryProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : LibraryProxy` is `liveLibrary` (`ElementId.fs:liveLibrary`) over `(LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase database).proxy`, `SampleProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 74) and `SourceProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 76): the live view composed once, reusing `liveLibrary` and its derived tree (step 47) with no logic of its own; it calls no EF Core API, so it carries no boundary mark. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: the `LibraryEntryStore` and `liveLibrary` docs name the database builders beside the in-memory store, in one line each. No cache, retry, lifecycle verb, protection rule or ordering option is added, and no product root composes the stores in this section (S2.4). (3) Tests, in `LibraryProxyTests.fs`: `type LibraryProxySqliteTests () = inherit LibraryProxyContract ()` runs the 10 contract facts (step 78): `liveStores` answers `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase`, `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` and `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, and `emptyPresetStore` answers `LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase` of a new `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString "Data Source=:memory:")` (step 62). The class implements `IDisposable` and disposes every database it opened. Its own facts: `the database preset store keeps detectors, polarizers and built-in sources, filed under their provenance`: over an empty database, `addEntry` of a `BuiltinCatalogue.sample` entry and of a `UserManaged` source under `newSourceId ()` each answers `PresetRefusedErr` and stores nothing; a `UserManaged` copy of `PresetIds.polarizerLp` under a fresh GUID id (`newSourceId ()`, step 20) is stored under `UserProvenance` and the intensity detector under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`), and both are offered for their kinds; and a user source saved through `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of the same database is neither offered for `LightSource` nor resolved by the preset store. `an inactive preset is not offered but still resolves`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, with `PresetIds.polarizerLp`'s latest version restaged `InactiveEntry` through `run`, `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer` answers `Ok []`, no leaf of the preset store's tree names it, and `tryGetEntry` still answers it. `the database live view offers a user source after the built-in sources and resolves it until it is removed`: over `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase` of `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, a user source saved through `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of the same database is the last `LightSource` entry, after exactly the catalogue's built-in sources (compared as a set, because the database orders them by name), resolves through `tryGetEntry`, and no longer resolves once removed. `a database failure below the preset store is LibraryUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database, `entriesForKind`, `libraryTrees`, `tryGetEntry` and `addEntry` of the preset store each answer `Error (LibraryUnavailableErr _)`.

**Acceptance.** After the database stores land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every LibraryProxyContract fact under `LibraryProxySqliteTests` and its own `the database preset store keeps detectors, polarizers and built-in sources, filed under their provenance`, `an inactive preset is not offered but still resolves`, `the database live view offers a user source after the built-in sources and resolves it until it is removed` and `a database failure below the preset store is LibraryUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 14; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.
